<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48913" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοάζω</span></b>  (A), (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοός</span> (A)) trans., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>move quickly, ply rapidly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτέρυγας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				1142
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ὅδ᾽ ἀγών . . θοάζων
				σε</span>; what task is thus <i>hurrying</i> thee <i>on?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Or.</u>
				335
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοάζω Βρομίῳ πόνον ἡδύν</span>
			<i>urge</i> it <i>on</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				65
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. σῖτα γένυσι</span>
			<i>dispatch</i> it <i>quickly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HF</u>
				382
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> intr.,
				<i>move quickly, rush, dart</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοάζων αἰθέρος ἄνω καπνός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1542
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δὲ δασκίοις ὄρεσι θ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				219
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. δρόμῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					307
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆτος θοάζον ἐξ Ἀτλαντικῆς ἁλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					145
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέω, θοός</span>
		(A).)</div>
